== compopt -o plusdirs adds the directories after the reply:
probe_dir/
probe_word
== compopt -o dirnames adds the directories to an empty reply:
probe_dir/
== compopt +o plusdirs drops the directories of the spec:
probe_word
== compopt prints the current options under the command name:
probe_dir/
probe_file
compopt +o bashdefault +o default +o dirnames +o filenames +o fullquote +o noquote +o nosort -o nospace +o plusdirs cp
== the registered spec keeps its options:
probe_dir/
probe_file
compopt +o bashdefault +o default +o dirnames -o filenames +o fullquote +o noquote +o nosort +o nospace +o plusdirs cp
== a compopt with a command operand inside the function changes the spec:
probe_dir/
probe_file
compopt +o bashdefault +o default +o dirnames +o filenames +o fullquote +o noquote +o nosort -o nospace +o plusdirs cp
== nosort keeps the reply order and drops only a repeated neighbor:
zeta
alpha
mid
zeta
== the reply is sorted and deduplicated without nosort:
alpha
mid
zeta
== a reply is quoted only with filenames or with fullquote:
a b
'a b'
a b
'a b'
'a b'
== noquote leaves the fallback filenames unquoted:
'spaced name'
spaced name
